    body: "Underscores is an infinite creative computational canvas for performance, teaching, exploration, and research. Drawing, code, sound, motion, physics, collaboration, and time share one document instead of living in separate tools. That document is called a patch.\n\nFour ideas carry most of the system. Everything visible is an ordinary canvas object you can select, move, group, and delete. A program is a Livecode node: one canvas object whose contents are running source. Physics is a relationship graph laid over objects you already drew, not a separate simulation window. Timeline supplies one shared clock, so drawings, programs, media, and sound can agree about when things happen.\n\nA patch saves as name.__.json, an Excalidraw-compatible file with an Underscores envelope. The canvas stays quiet: controls live in dockable panels you open when you need them, and every action is a registered command that the palette, the assistant, History, Playlist, and guided walkthroughs all share.",
